            <ArticleTitle>Postsynthetic N-methylation making a metal-organic framework responsive to alkylamines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1747-1750</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10278f</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The postsynthetically created electron-deficient 2,2'-bipyridinium moieties in a Zr-MOF provide charge-transfer interacting sites for recognizing and capturing alkylamines with excellent selectivity; meanwhile the MOF shows fast and reversible vapochromism and luminescence quenching in response to alkyamines.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
